[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5781321596","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123703#issuecomment-5781321596","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123703","id":5781321596,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWJf3fA","user":{"login":"jack-klein-5","id":56490766,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NDkwNzY2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56490766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jack-klein-5","html_url":"https://github.com/jack-klein-5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jack-klein-5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jack-klein-5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jack-klein-5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jack-klein-5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jack-klein-5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jack-klein-5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jack-klein-5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jack-klein-5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jack-klein-5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-22T17:53:14Z","updated_at":"2026-09-22T17:53:14Z","body":"The problem here isn't a bug with Godot but rather how you're setting the column minimum width. Tree items have a start margin called `h_separation` that's being used here, which is pushing your text to the right and cutting it off. To correct it, you can add it to your minimum width like this:\n`tree.set_column_custom_minimum_width(1, ceili(time_size.x) + tree.get_theme_constant(&\"h_separation\"))\n tree.set_column_custom_minimum_width(2, ceili(calls_size.x) + tree.get_theme_constant(&\"h_separation\"))`\nOr you can change the theme on your tree, Constants->H Separation to 0 to get rid of the start margin.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5781321596/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5782399988","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123703#issuecomment-5782399988","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123703","id":5782399988,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWKhr9A","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-22T19:10:19Z","updated_at":"2026-09-22T19:14:02Z","body":"> The problem here isn't a bug with Godot but rather how you're setting the column minimum width. Tree items have a start margin called `h_separation` that's being used here, which is pushing your text to the right and cutting it off.\n\nI'm not sure why I should know about all the margins when setting a minimum width for a column. These margins are computed internally and should be taken into account automatically without user's input because they are theme constants. And because it's called \"separation\" it's even more weird than if it was just margins.\n\nIf maintainers think that this behavior is desirable then it should be noted in the docs.\n\nUPD. Theme item description says \"The horizontal space between item cells. This is also used as the margin at the start of an item when folding is disabled\". Which makes it even more confusing for how should a user know when it's used or not.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5782399988/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5790709043","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123703#issuecomment-5790709043","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123703","id":5790709043,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWSc1Mw","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-23T07:18:30Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T07:18:40Z","body":"So I think it's a combination of `h_separation` + `item_margin`. And as they are not accounted for in the internal code I think that's why for example in the Profiler the text from the Name column overlaps the text from the Time column:\n\n<img width=\"361\" height=\"370\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0afc4857-4620-4dfd-af7a-70b7f4537320\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5790709043/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]